<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uzana I of Pinya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1325">1325</a>–<a href="/years/1340">1340</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uzana I was king of Pinya in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1325 to 1340, a son of the Pagan king Kyawswa and stepson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thihathu">Thihathu</a>, founder of Pinya. Thihathu's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saw-yun">Saw Yun</a> had already broken away to found the rival kingdom of Sagaing in 1315, and Uzana ruled the southern part of the divided realm. He gave up the throne in 1340.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Uzana I</b> and Kyawswa I were among its kings.</blockquote><a href="/state/pinya-kingdom">Pinya Kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Pinle, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. Died in Mekkhaya, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.5,96&amp;year=1332" aria-label="Pinle on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7128 1369 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Uzana I of Pinya"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7578 1639h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7578 1639h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.5,96&amp;year=1332">What was here in 1332? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
